    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b9803dacd86a2706fed4187f05805d0a128c108eb185eb1467f0e237d9247ec5",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Reality reorganizes both formal long expansions around stationary cutoffs. For the Hardy Z-function, truncation near the stationary Dirichlet term makes the resummed tail conjugate to the early terms; fractional-cutoff corrections repair discontinuity, and factorial late terms determine least-term truncation and exponentially small error. For a real quantum spectral determinant, the corresponding composite pseudo-orbit expansion is stationary at half the Heisenberg time, so analytic continuation approximately pairs long and short groups. An alternative Erfc smoothing, distinct from the untransferred Riemann-Siegel coefficient series, supplies the quantum lookalike's transferable completion.",
