    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f68f7f369da52ca324004d07af5887da98526429c8f0c3ded982101f1aa1d94a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source gives a layered mechanism for universal and nonuniversal zero statistics. Exponential orbit proliferation balances squared-amplitude decay, so the diagonal form factor becomes universal before the Heisenberg time; discreteness forces off-diagonal coherence afterward, and Hardy-Littlewood prime-pair correlations conditionally supply it for the zeros. Short-orbit terms and noninvariant dynamical-zeta structure then restore system-specific corrections, with zeta near one making low zeros reappear as resonances in high-zero correlations.",
