    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fc3914c10749d43afe04756a5e50ecbd4d603d874962d48d4f8ca04e1c0db09d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Placing the prime-power expansion of the zero-counting fluctuation beside the semiclassical periodic-orbit expansion yields a constrained dictionary: primes label primitive periods log p, powers label repetitions, coefficient matching imposes unit instability and broken time-reversal symmetry, and comparison with mean spacing sets the prime or orbit scale needed for level resolution. The later density comparison then turns exact-amplitude and fixed-sign discrepancies into obstructions to a literal realization.",
